A||||14||87GT||What do you all think?||||5||
Z||000000||87GT||02-29-2000||07:57 PM||||Hello all.  I am seriously considering getting a new paint job on my fiero.  Right now it is maroon with grey trim.  The paint on it is in pretty good shape except its oxidizing on the top of the passenger door and a little bit on the deck lid.  My question is, Do you all think I should keep it the original maroon/grey or not?  I really am thinking about painting it white/black trim.  I also am going to get "Fiero GT" lettering in black to match the trim and go on both doors.  I also want to get a black pegasus logo to put on the hood. I am probably going to start the process in the next month.  I plan on replacing the quarter windowns and all the molding.  Let me know what you all think of the paint scheming.  Thanks!||||reg||5
Z||000001||Gokart||02-29-2000||08:19 PM||||Hey Kyle! Your GT looks just like mine except you got those sweet mecham scoops. I love the medium red color and would not paint over it with white. You'd probably have a hard time finding a shop to paint it a lighter color. Around these parts I can't find a bodyshop that wants to paint my car unless it's the same color or darker. I asked cause personally, the only color I would paint over the red is yellow with black trim. The Fiero GT on the doors and pegasus decal will look awesome, but I wouldn't go with white. It's just too WHITE! My all-time favorite Fiero picture <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/ViewPhoto?u=29019&a=173024&p=10529780" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/ViewPhoto?u=29019&a=173024&p=10529780</A>  check it out!<p>[This message has been edited by Gokart (edited 02-29-2000).]||||reg||6
Z||000002||Phil||02-29-2000||09:34 PM||||I had my red coupe changed to yellow but the paint shop sanded all the red off first||||reg||1
Z||000003||stimpy||02-29-2000||09:43 PM||||To each their own.  I personally don't care for the large decals on the body. They really do not age well and are kinda eighties looking. I actually think the dark red looks really good when it is shined.  Since the paint would need to be taken down before painting, might i suggest a good wet sand job? I think you will find that the milky white oxidation that you have is just dead clearcoat, and you will be left with a really nice "20 foot"paint job for the cost of a few hours work.||||reg||1
